      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While I acknowledge the concerns about biases and disparities, if I had topick a single most equitable standard, it would be the lottery system. A random lottery can provide a level ofblindness to subjective judgments, reducing the potential for discriminatory biases and unequal treatment. This approach would treat all applicants equally, regardless of their income levels, location, or social status, and would be transparent and less prone to administrative errors.",
      "source": "target",
